# Onderon, the ruined Merchant Quarter and the Sky Ramp (TSL, 511OND,
# 504OND, 506OND): the Basilisk landed among Vaklu's troops (the
# Royalist soldier's alarm), the troops fought, Captain Bostuco's word that
# the Sky Ramp is overrun and Talia, Kavar and Kadron's scene in the
# Palace; up the Sky Ramp: the first platform's troopers, the barracks
# retaken (the Royalist Sergeant sends two men after the Exile), the Turret
# Control Tower's door [Security]ed, its console: Bostuco's access code,
# the lower force shield deactivated; the troopers at the shield told to surrender, Bostuco on
# the second shield, the fleeing cowards let go ("I will not harm you if
# you leave now"), the damaged upper shield bashed through with the saber,
# the Sith Lords and turrets at the top, into the Royal Palace.
# Starts from the Basilisk's landing:
#   kjk playthrough tsl @onderon_civil_war data/routes/tsl/finale_sky_ramp.route --god
# Walkthrough: DSimpson's "Onderon Civil War" and "The Sky Ramp";
# GameBanshee 48 and 51 (context/walkthroughs/tsl/).
# The tower's turret (term_acc's "Control the turret.", 505OND) is manned
# once the shield is down.
# Left: the barracks' lockers and
# workbench, the power conductors (xterm1, xterm2: they blow up on the
# party).
#
# ASSUMES:
# - The party is the Exile, Kreia and Mandalore (finale_sith_tomb).
# - Bostuco's scenes in 511OND (cs_tal_3 starts 1, 2, 3) play at
#   tr_cs_tal_3; Bostuco then runs ahead to the Sky Ramp.
# - 511OND's To_504 links From_510OND, which 504OND does not have: the
#   arrival falls back on 504OND's entry (78.7, 16.2), by From_502OND.
# - door_tower is Locked (OpenLockDC 28, no key): the Exile's Security.
# - term_acc start 0 (c_local_notset and c_global_eq) offers Bostuco's code;
#   once in, "Deactivate forceshield barrier." (a_kill_barrier).
# - ffield_upper (KeyRequired, Locked; Hardness 125: a permanent damage
#   resistance of 125 against every damage type but base damage,
#   CSWSDoor::PostProcess) stays up on the Queen's side (a_kill_barrier
#   opens it only for Vaklu's); Bao-Dur, whose blow opens it
#   (a_ffield_baodur), is on Dxun, so the saber bashes it, Bostuco's way:
#   a blow worth more than its hardness (--mighty's).
say The Mandalorian exploits have left a profound impact # ro_sold, Mandalore
talk                 # "A Basilisk? A Basilisk here?" (k_511_enter)
to tr_cs_tal_3       # Bostuco; Talia, Kavar and Kadron in the Palace (cs_tal_3)
talk                 # (its last lines: "This way, this way to the Sky Ramp!")
fight 40             # Vaklu's troops in the Merchant Quarter
exit To_504
module 504ond
to tr_trooper1       # ro_trp1: "A Jedi... here? Men, attack!"
talk
fight 40
use door_barrack     # the barracks (k_barrack_open)
fight 30
use RepSold          # ro_brck: "Hold your fire, they're with us!"; two follow
unlock door_tower    # the Turret Control Tower ([Security], DC 28)
use door_tower
fight 30             # the tower's troops
say Enter Bostuco's access code. # term_acc start 0
say Deactivate forceshield barrier.
use term_acc
say Control the turret. # term_acc again: 505OND, the tower's gun
use term_acc
turrets              # the eight fighters (800 XP), back at From_505OND
to tr_trooper2       # ro_trp2 at the lower shield
say Surrender now. Why lose your life for General Vaklu's ambitions?
talk
fight 40
to tr_bost_2         # Bostuco: the second force shield, damaged
talk
fight 40             # the mines and the ramp's troopers
say I will not harm you if you leave now. # ro_trp3: the cowards let go
to tr_trooper3
talk
fight 40             # the Sith Lord who cut them down, his line
bash ffield_upper    # the damaged upper force shield, by the saber (Bostuco's "bash
                     # your way through it"; its Hardness a resistance of 125)
fight 40
to tr_officer_3      # the top platform: Sith Lords and turrets
fight 40
exit To_506
module 506ond
save onderon_royal_palace
